---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CodeExample from "../../components/CodeExample.astro";
import PageIntro from "../../components/PageIntro.astro";
import { SITE } from "../../consts";
import lessonSource from "../../generated/examples/tutorial-expressions-and-decisions.kwe?raw";

const source = lessonSource.trimEnd();
const output = "16\neziokwu\nụgha\neziokwu\neziokwu\neziokwu\nOkenye";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Lesson 3: Expressions and Decisions"
  description="Learn Kwechiri arithmetic, comparisons, Boolean logic, and conditional decisions."
>
  <PageIntro
    eyebrow="Tutorial 03"
    title="Expressions and Decisions"
    lead="Calculate values, compare them, combine Boolean results, and choose which block of a program should run."
    meta="Beginner · Complete Lesson 2 first"
  />

  <div class="shell content-layout">
    <nav class="docs-nav" aria-label="Tutorial navigation">
      <a href="/tutorials/variables-and-values/">← Lesson 2: Variables and Values</a>
      <a href="/tutorials/expressions-and-decisions/" aria-current="page">Lesson 3: Expressions and decisions</a>
      <a href="/tutorials/repetition-and-loop-control/">Lesson 4: Repetition and loop control</a>
      <span>Functions · Planned</span>
    </nav>
    <article class="prose">
      <h2>The program</h2>
      <p>Open <code>examples/tutorials/expressions-and-decisions.kwe</code>.</p>
      <CodeExample label="examples/tutorials/expressions-and-decisions.kwe" code={source} output={output} />

      <h2>Run it</h2>
      <pre tabindex="0"><code>node dist/cli/index.js examples/tutorials/expressions-and-decisions.kwe</code></pre>

      <h2>Arithmetic</h2>
      <p>
        Kwechiri currently provides <code>+</code>, <code>-</code>, <code>*</code>,
        and <code>/</code> for numbers. Multiplication and division happen
        before addition and subtraction. Parentheses override that order.
      </p>
      <pre tabindex="0"><code>nsonaazụ = (3 + 5) * 2
# 16</code></pre>
      <p>
        Arithmetic does not accept strings, and <code>+</code> does not
        concatenate strings. Dividing by zero is a runtime error.
      </p>

      <h2>Comparisons</h2>
      <p>
        <code>&lt;</code>, <code>&lt;=</code>, <code>&gt;</code>, and
        <code>&gt;=</code> compare numbers. <code>==</code> and
        <code>!=</code> compare supported primitive values without converting
        types. Comparisons produce <code>eziokwu</code> or <code>ụgha</code>.
      </p>

      <h2>Boolean logic</h2>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Operator</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>na</code></td><td>and</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>maọbụ</code></td><td>or</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>ọ bụghị</code></td><td>not</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>
        These operators accept booleans only. <code>na</code> and
        <code>maọbụ</code> evaluate left to right and short-circuit. Kwechiri
        does not treat numbers, strings, collections, or <code>efu</code> as
        automatic truth values.
      </p>

      <h2>Conditions</h2>
      <pre tabindex="0"><code>ọ bụrụ (afọ >= 18) &#123;
    ọkwa = "Okenye"
&#125; ọzọ &#123;
    ọkwa = "Nwatakịrị"
&#125;</code></pre>
      <p>
        The condition must be Boolean. Exactly one branch runs. Because both
        branches assign <code>ọkwa</code> as a string, that name is available
        after the condition.
      </p>

      <h2>Your turn</h2>
      <p>
        Change the first line to <code>afọ = 16</code> and predict the output
        before running the program. Then replace <code>na</code> with
        <code>maọbụ</code> in the first logical expression and explain why
        the result is still <code>eziokwu</code>.
      </p>

      <div class="callout callout--gold">
        <strong>Common problems</strong>
        Parentheses control grouping. Use <code>==</code> for equality and
        <code>=</code> for assignment. A name created in only one branch is
        unavailable after the condition.
      </div>

      <h2>Normative references</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href={`${SITE.github}/blob/main/docs/language-spec/expressions.md`}>Expressions</a></li>
        <li><a href={`${SITE.github}/blob/main/docs/language-spec/control-flow.md`}>Control flow</a></li>
        <li><a href={`${SITE.github}/blob/main/docs/language-spec/errors.md`}>Current language errors</a></li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Next</h2>
      <p>
        Continue with
        <a href="/tutorials/repetition-and-loop-control/">Lesson 4: Repetition and Loop Control</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
